	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["0B23279463D8A784"]
			description: [
				"&3&lPneumaticCraft: Repressurized&r runs on &eair&r, not FE."
				""
				"Every machine you have built so far takes a cable and eats energy. These do not. They take a &epressure tube&r and they eat &eatmosphere&r - and if you push too much in, they &cexplode&r."
				""
				"&7That trade is the whole mod. Air is cheap and easy to make; storing it safely is the hard part, and every machine here has a pressure ceiling you can exceed.&r"
				""
				"&8AE2 gave you a network that builds anything you can already craft. This chapter is about making the things a crafting table cannot.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:air_compressor"
			id: "5F1B17DE5A751804"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "574D240493274CFF"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 50
				}
				{
					id: "27775D25577698E7"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Air is the new cable"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0B776C721652B9E8"
				title: "Begin PneumaticCraft"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&3Pressure, Not Power"
			x: -9.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5F1B17DE5A751804"]
			description: [
				"The mod's starting material, and it is made by &cblowing up iron&r."
				""
				"&e&lHow:&r drop iron ingots on the ground and detonate TNT next to them. The blast compresses what it does not destroy. Expect losses - that is normal and intended."
				""
				"&7Once you have a Pressure Chamber this becomes a clean, lossless recipe. Until then, explosives are the only route, so make a batch big enough to build the chamber itself.&r"
				""
				"&8The item id is &7ingot_iron_compressed&8, not compressed_iron_ingot - worth knowing if you are searching JEI.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:ingot_iron_compressed"
			id: "476FCEE0C4E3BB61"
			rewards: [{
				id: "71F25A6B779D738F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Blow up iron on purpose"
			tasks: [{
				count: 8L
				id: "4DA0D23441732063"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:ingot_iron_compressed"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Compressed Iron"
			x: -7.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Burns solid fuel to make &epressurised air&r. This is your first pressure source."
				""
				"&7Feed it coal, charcoal or anything else that burns. It fills whatever is connected to it through pressure tubes.&r"
				""
				"&e&lWatch the gauge.&r An Air Compressor will happily keep pumping past the safe limit of whatever it is attached to. Pressure that exceeds a machine's rating destroys the machine - and a Pressure Chamber failing at full pressure takes the room with it."
				""
				"&8There are better compressors later - Advanced, Liquid, Flux, Electrostatic, Solar. This one is deliberately crude.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:air_compressor"
			id: "4E6385AC3D47904B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "500D8D22C3F3FBC8"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Burn fuel, make air"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5FC9232C4C4FAEDC"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:air_compressor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3The Air Compressor"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4E6385AC3D47904B"]
			description: [
				"Air moves through &epressure tubes&r, and it equalises across everything they connect."
				""
				"&7There is no direction and no throughput rating - one connected network shares one pressure value. A compressor at one end raises the pressure everywhere at once.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThat means one over-pressurised machine can be caused by a compressor three rooms away.&r Keep separate pressure networks for machines with different limits, or regulate between them."
				""
				"&8Tube modules clip onto tubes and are where most of the mod's control lives - regulators, safety valves, pressure gauges, redstone logic.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:pressure_tube"
			id: "27FE2D3D678A6B43"
			rewards: [{
				id: "61D7BDD570FB1124"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7One network, one pressure"
			tasks: [{
				count: 8L
				id: "36A01FC5DC149958"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:pressure_tube"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Pressure Tubes"
			x: -4.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["27FE2D3D678A6B43"]
			description: [
				"&c&lRead this before you build anything expensive.&r"
				""
				"A &eSafety Tube Module&r vents air once pressure passes a threshold you set. It is the difference between a machine that stops and a machine that detonates."
				""
				"&7A &ePressure Gauge Module&r shows the current value on the tube itself, so you can see a problem building instead of discovering it.&r"
				""
				"&e&lA Regulator Tube Module&r caps how much pressure flows onward - use it to run a 5-bar machine off a 20-bar network safely."
				""
				"&8Every explosion in this mod is preventable and almost all of them are caused by skipping this quest.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:safety_tube_module"
			id: "15331FCA574312E1"
			rewards: [{
				id: "74F2F9BD08041B32"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Cheaper than rebuilding"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "6CBEDDA90ABDF5BF"
					item: "pneumaticcraft:pressure_gauge"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "3EAE27845D597A97"
					item: "pneumaticcraft:safety_tube_module"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&3Gauges and Safety Valves"
			x: -3.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["27FE2D3D678A6B43"]
			description: [
				"A hollow cube of chamber walls with at least one &eValve&r and one &eInterface&r. Pressurise it and it crafts."
				""
				"&e&lBuild:&r a 3x3x3 (or larger) shell - walls, glass for visibility, one valve, one interface for item in/out. The inside must be empty."
				""
				"&7This is where Compressed Iron stops needing TNT. Throw iron in, raise the pressure, get compressed iron out with no losses. It also makes the plastic feedstock and several parts you cannot get any other way.&r"
				""
				"&8Bigger chambers hold more items but need more air to reach the same pressure. 4x4x4 is a comfortable working size.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:pressure_chamber_valve"
			id: "114109F9E95F5341"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "5350BBB3808DF05E"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 60
				}
				{
					id: "73D1FC1852E1D645"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "&7Craft with atmosphere"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "01324E6F5EC85D7E"
					item: "pneumaticcraft:pressure_chamber_valve"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 8L
					id: "002F609FFCA609CA"
					item: "pneumaticcraft:pressure_chamber_wall"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&3The Pressure Chamber"
			x: -1.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["114109F9E95F5341"]
			description: [
				"PneumaticCraft's chemistry starts with &ecrude oil&r."
				""
				"&7On a skyblock there is no oil lake to pump, so you make it: a &eGas Lift&r on a deep enough shaft, or far more practically, let another mod's oil feed the same tag.&r"
				""
				"&e&lWhat oil is for:&r the Refinery cracks it into Diesel, Kerosene, LPG and Gasoline. Those are fuels, but more importantly LPG and Diesel are what the Thermopneumatic Processing Plant turns into &ePlastic&r."
				""
				"&8Plastic is the wall between you and every circuit in this mod. Everything below this quest depends on getting oil flowing.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:oil_bucket"
			id: "2C9F3C747B643CE8"
			rewards: [{
				id: "37B9836455FB6801"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The feedstock for everything"
			tasks: [{
				id: "12F04419A34F4D93"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:oil_bucket"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Oil"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2C9F3C747B643CE8"]
			description: [
				"Stack &eRefinery&r blocks vertically and heat them. Oil goes in the bottom; different fractions come out at different heights."
				""
				"&7Two blocks tall gives you Diesel and LPG. Three gives Kerosene as well. Four gives Gasoline. Taller stacks are strictly better - build four.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt needs heat, not pressure.&r Feed it from a heat source - lava, a Vortex Tube's hot side, or a heating element. The hotter it runs, the faster it refines."
				""
				"&8All four outputs must have somewhere to go. A full output tank stalls the whole stack.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:refinery"
			id: "54256C29EAFD9893"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1C856909C42ACBE0"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Crack oil into fuels"
			tasks: [{
				count: 3L
				id: "619F7CB4F3A89FDB"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:refinery"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3The Refinery"
			x: 1.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["54256C29EAFD9893"]
			description: [
				"A &eVortex Tube&r takes pressurised air and splits it into a &chot&r end and a &bcold&r end. No fuel, no power - just pressure."
				""
				"&7That hot end is how you heat a Refinery or a Thermopneumatic Processing Plant without burning anything. The cold end is how you freeze things later.&r"
				""
				"&e&lHeat Sinks&r move heat away from something that is getting too hot. Machines in this mod have a temperature as well as a pressure, and both can kill them."
				""
				"&8Heat spreads between touching blocks. Sinks, frames and the tube all care about what they are physically next to.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:vortex_tube"
			id: "43398E3A1581BE26"
			rewards: [{
				id: "05E9E632DFFBC6C8"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Hot and cold from air alone"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "27F25CAE81BC2C3E"
					item: "pneumaticcraft:vortex_tube"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 2L
					id: "3ABB78859ACF2252"
					item: "pneumaticcraft:heat_sink"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&3Heat and the Vortex Tube"
			x: 1.5d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["54256C29EAFD9893"]
			description: [
				"&eThermopneumatic Processing Plant&r: LPG plus heat plus pressure gives you molten plastic, which cools into sheets."
				""
				"&7This is the single most important item in the mod. Printed Circuit Boards need it, drones need it, every machine past this point needs it.&r"
				""
				"&e&lSet up a loop, not a batch.&r Oil to Refinery to LPG to Processing Plant to Plastic, running continuously. You will need hundreds of sheets and hand-feeding it is miserable."
				""
				"&8Plastic comes in colours. They are purely decorative except where a recipe names one - and a few do, so keep the white ones.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:plastic"
			id: "3316E24A3B26354B"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "47F7DB4F8FB8895C"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 60
				}
				{
					id: "3876A2EF40AB465F"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "&7The wall you have to climb"
			tasks: [{
				count: 16L
				id: "4367833132BE8A9A"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:plastic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Plastic"
			x: 3.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3316E24A3B26354B"]
			description: [
				"The machine that made your plastic - and it does considerably more than that."
				""
				"&7It combines a fluid, heat and pressure into something new. Plastic is the obvious product; it also makes Etching Acid, which is the next quest, and several intermediate chemicals.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt needs all three inputs in range at once.&r Too cold and nothing happens. Too hot and you waste air. The recipe tooltip in JEI lists the temperature band each recipe wants."
				""
				"&8Pair it permanently with a Vortex Tube and a Refinery - the three of them together are the chemical core of your base.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:thermopneumatic_processing_plant"
			id: "547837702F80246F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1AA1ED484D7909BE"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Fluid plus heat plus air"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3456C2828F2691EB"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:thermopneumatic_processing_plant"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Thermopneumatic Processing Plant"
			x: 3.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3316E24A3B26354B"]
			description: [
				"The most involved thing you have crafted so far, and a genuine multi-step process."
				""
				"&e&l1.&r &7Empty PCB&r in a &eUV Light Box&r - exposes it. Watch the progress bar; over-exposing ruins it."
				"&e&l2.&r Drop the exposed board in an &eEtching Tank&r full of &eEtching Acid&r."
				"&e&l3.&r Out comes an &eUnassembled PCB&r - or a &cFailed PCB&r if you got the exposure wrong."
				"&e&l4.&r Failed boards are not waste: reprocess them to recover most of the material."
				""
				"&7Assemble the unassembled board with a transistor and a capacitor to finish it.&r"
				""
				"&8This is deliberately fiddly by hand. The Assembly Line exists to do it for you - which is the next quest, and the point of this whole chapter.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:printed_circuit_board"
			id: "65B80864358094A0"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "4A5666143E31F661"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 70
				}
				{
					id: "27AA71AAAAB74651"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "&7Expose, etch, assemble"
			tasks: [{
				count: 4L
				id: "71BB9D5FB36D8377"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:printed_circuit_board"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Printed Circuit Boards"
			x: 4.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&3&lRobotic arms that build things a crafting table cannot.&r"
				""
				"A row of machines under an &eAssembly Controller&r: a &ePlatform&r to hold the work, a &eDrill&r and a &eLaser&r to shape it, and &eIO Units&r to feed and collect."
				""
				"&e&lThey must be in a line and all touching the controller's row.&r Give the controller the right &eProgram&r - Drill, Laser, or Drill+Laser - for the recipe you want."
				""
				"&7This is the first machine in the pack that performs a recipe no crafting grid can express. It is also the reason PneumaticCraft sits between AE2 and GregTech: it teaches automated assembly on a small scale, right before GregTech demands it on a large one.&r"
				""
				"&8Point an AE2 Pattern Provider at the import unit and your ME network can drive the whole thing.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:assembly_controller"
			id: "6800E30C46DE556B"
			rewards: [
