		{
			dependencies: ["6800E30C46DE556B"]
			description: [
				"A &eDrone&r is a flying robot you &eprogram&r rather than configure."
				""
				"&e&lHow:&r put a drone in a &eProgrammer&r and drag puzzle-piece instructions together - go here, pick up that, place it there, repeat. It is a visual programming language and it is genuinely powerful."
				""
				"&7Drones dig, build, farm, fight, move fluids and haul items between places nothing else will reach. They run on air, so they need a charging station and a pressure supply.&r"
				""
				"&8Start with something small - a drone that empties one chest into another - before attempting a quarry. The debugging tools are good but the learning curve is real.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:drone"
			id: "0AD14E5D12410C2F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "33E73B1F1D0BA58B"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 60
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Program it, do not configure it"
			tasks: [{
				id: "21D0B8051C94C2AB"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:drone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Drones"
			x: 7.5d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6800E30C46DE556B"]
			description: [
				"Drones, pneumatic armour and pneumatic tools all hold air, and all need somewhere to refill."
				""
				"&7Place a &eCharging Station&r on a pressurised tube and drop the item on top. Add an &eUpgrade&r slot module to charge faster.&r"
				""
				"&8The station also charges items in a player's inventory if they stand on it - handy next to the door.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:charging_station"
			id: "64E7B4BEB420192D"
