			}]
			title: "&3Charging Station"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0AD14E5D12410C2F"]
			description: [
				"A drone that never moves. It sits in one block and runs a drone program from there."
				""
				"&7Cheaper than a real drone, cannot be shot down, and perfect for a fixed job - restocking a machine, harvesting one farm, keeping a tank topped up.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt has a limited working radius&r, so it replaces logistics inside a room rather than across a base."
				""
				"&8If you find yourself writing the same drone program for a job that never moves, this is the block you actually wanted.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:programmable_controller"
			id: "2E123689C466249B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "679E90A7CDDCFBF2"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7A drone that stays put"
			tasks: [{
				id: "772FBA90BEF94853"
				item: "pneumaticcraft:programmable_controller"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&3Programmable Controller"
			x: 9.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0AD14E5D12410C2F"]
			description: [
				"Item routing with no pipes and no cables at all."
				""
				"&7Stick &eLogistics Frames&r on inventories - Provider, Requester, Storage - and a &eLogistics Drone&r flies the items between them. Configure with the &eLogistics Configurator&r.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt crosses gaps nothing else does&r - between floating islands, across a room, through a wall you never want to run a pipe through."
				""
				"&8Slower than pipes but vastly easier to reconfigure. Good for low-volume, awkward routes.&r"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:logistics_drone"
			id: "1EAE763F48B86557"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2026DC207400CF45"
